doc:sch-1-sec-5e-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "5E(1) Serious contraventions" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Act, a serious contravention is a contravention of a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory that:  (a) is a serious offence; or  (b) is an offence punishable:  (i) by imprisonment for a period, or a maximum period, of at least 3 years; or  (ii) if the offence is committed by an individual—by a fine, or a maximum fine, of at least 180 penalty units; or  (iii) if the offence cannot be committed by an individual— by a fine, or a maximum fine, of at least 900 penalty units; or  (c) could, if established, render the person committing the contravention liable:  (i) if the contravention were committed by an individual— to pay a pecuniary penalty of 180 penalty units or more,  Stored communications  Schedule 1 Principal amendments  Part 1  Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   5 or to pay an amount that is the monetary equivalent of 180 penalty units or more; or  (ii) if the contravention cannot be committed by an individual—to pay a pecuniary penalty of 900 penalty units or more, or to pay an amount that is the monetary equivalent of 900 penalty units or more." ;
    cof:pageNumber "8"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-5e-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "5E(2) Serious contraventions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-5e-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Except so far as the contrary intention appears, a contravention, or a contravention of a particular kind, is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to be a contravention, or to be a contravention of that kind, as the case may be, that:  (a) has been committed or is being committed; or  (b) is suspected on reasonable grounds of having been committed, of being committed or of being likely to be committed." ;
    skos:definition "(2) Except so far as the contrary intention appears, a contravention, or a contravention of a particular kind, is taken, for the purposes of this Act, to be a contravention, or to be a contravention of that kind, as the case may be, that:  (a) has been committed or is being committed; or  (b) is suspected on reasonable grounds of having been committed, of being committed or of being likely to be committed."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "32ad76634182b6ff75597a0a6913b6c787af75f39f74555ec0bd45d5e8fbcab6" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-5e ;
    cof:pageNumber "8"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Communication from AFP must not start passing over a telecommunications system until it is no longer under control of specified employees. A contravention is taken to be a contravention if it has been committed or is suspected on reasonable grounds of having been committed." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.8" ;
    cml:asserts concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-5e-ss-2-norm .
