doc:sch-1-sec-5e-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "5E(1) Serious contraventions" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Act, a communication:  (a) is taken to start passing over a telecommunications system when it is sent or transmitted by the person sending the communication; and  (b) is taken to continue to pass over the system until it becomes accessible to the intended recipient of the communication." ;
    cof:pageNumber "8"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-5e-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "5E(2) Serious contraventions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-5e-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) However, if a communication is sent from an address on a computer network operated by or on behalf of the Australian Federal Police, it is taken not to start passing over a telecommunications system, for the purposes of this Act, until it is no longer under the control of any of the following:  (a) any AFP employee responsible for operating, protecting and maintaining the network;  (b) any AFP employee responsible for enforcement of the professional standards of the Australian Federal Police.  Schedule 1  Stored communications" ;
    skos:definition "(2) However, if a communication is sent from an address on a computer network operated by or on behalf of the Australian Federal Police, it is taken not to start passing over a telecommunications system, for the purposes of this Act, until it is no longer under the control of any of the following:  (a) any AFP employee responsible for operating, protecting and maintaining the network;  (b) any AFP employee responsible for enforcement of the professional standards of the Australian Federal Police.  Schedule 1  Stored communications"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "40eb06cfd914f4e042b320f0c168f4cf063e73227185333e4c5f3b1e4c38b4db" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-5e ;
    cof:pageNumber "8"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Communication from AFP must not start passing over a telecommunications system until it is no longer under control of specified employees. A contravention is taken to be a contravention if it has been committed or is suspected on reasonable grounds of having been committed." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.8" ;
    cml:asserts concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-5e-ss-2-norm .
