doc:sch-1-sec-5g-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "5G(1) The intended recipient of a communication" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Act, the intended recipient of a communication is:  (a) if the communication is addressed to an individual (either in the individual’s own capacity or in the capacity of an employee or agent of another person)—the individual; or  (b) if the communication is addressed to a person who is not an individual—the person; or  (c) if the communication is not addressed to a person—the person who has, or whose employee or agent has, control over the telecommunications service to which the communication is sent." ;
    cof:pageNumber "10"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-5g-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "5G(2) The intended recipient of a communication"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-5g-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) In addition to the person who is the intended recipient of a communication under subsection (1), if a communication is addressed to a person at an address on a computer network operated by or on behalf of the Australian Federal Police, each of the following is also an intended recipient of the communication for the purposes of this Act:  (a) any AFP employee responsible for operating, protecting and maintaining the network;  (b) any AFP employee responsible for enforcement of the professional standards of the Australian Federal Police." ;
    skos:definition "(2) In addition to the person who is the intended recipient of a communication under subsection (1), if a communication is addressed to a person at an address on a computer network operated by or on behalf of the Australian Federal Police, each of the following is also an intended recipient of the communication for the purposes of this Act:  (a) any AFP employee responsible for operating, protecting and maintaining the network;  (b) any AFP employee responsible for enforcement of the professional standards of the Australian Federal Police."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b1f6fa4e41eaf85f1f7af108c8a86d4dbd47b4e07c3eb5c4131551fdd60bfabf" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-5g ;
    cof:pageNumber "10"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Intended recipients of a communication addressed to an AFP employee or the Australian Federal Police. No limitation on accessibility for the purposes of this Act." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
