concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-8 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "8 Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-8 ;
    values:originalText "(a) a judge of a court created by the Parliament; or  (b) a Federal Magistrate; or  (c) a magistrate; may, by writing, consent to be appointed by the Minister under subsection (1).  (3) A person’s appointment ceases to have effect if:  (a) the person ceases to be a person whom the Minister could appoint under this section; or  (b) the Minister, by writing, revokes the appointment.  (4) An issuing authority has, in relation to the performance or exercise of a function or power conferred on an issuing authority by this Act, the same protection and immunity as a Justice of the High Court has in relation to proceedings in the High Court." ;
    skos:definition "(a) a judge of a court created by the Parliament; or  (b) a Federal Magistrate; or  (c) a magistrate; may, by writing, consent to be appointed by the Minister under subsection (1).  (3) A person’s appointment ceases to have effect if:  (a) the person ceases to be a person whom the Minister could appoint under this section; or  (b) the Minister, by writing, revokes the appointment.  (4) An issuing authority has, in relation to the performance or exercise of a function or power conferred on an issuing authority by this Act, the same protection and immunity as a Justice of the High Court has in relation to proceedings in the High Court."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2695136c1a8fd2a3371dd5d1477dea0bae908a4b7e679d8e89f84c84ab2d641f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "12"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-8-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-8-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.12" .
doc:sch-1-sec-8 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "8 Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(a) a judge of a court created by the Parliament; or  (b) a Federal Magistrate; or  (c) a magistrate; may, by writing, consent to be appointed by the Minister under subsection (1).  (3) A person’s appointment ceases to have effect if:  (a) the person ceases to be a person whom the Minister could appoint under this section; or  (b) the Minister, by writing, revokes the appointment.  (4) An issuing authority has, in relation to the performance or exercise of a function or power conferred on an issuing authority by this Act, the same protection and immunity as a Justice of the High Court has in relation to proceedings in the High Court." ;
    cof:pageNumber "12"^^xsd:integer .

