    values:originalText "(3) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(b), access to a stored communication is taken to be under an interception warrant if, and only if, the warrant would have authorised interception of the communication if it were still passing over a telecommunications system." ;
    cof:pageNumber "14"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-10-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10(4) Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-10-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) In determining, for the purposes of paragraphs (2)(d) and (e), whether an act or thing done by a person was reasonably necessary in order for the person to perform his or her duties effectively, a court is to have regard to such matters (if any) as are specified in, or ascertained in accordance with, the regulations. Note: The civil remedy provisions in Part 3-7 may apply to a contravention of this section.  Schedule 1  Stored communications" ;
    skos:definition "(4) In determining, for the purposes of paragraphs (2)(d) and (e), whether an act or thing done by a person was reasonably necessary in order for the person to perform his or her duties effectively, a court is to have regard to such matters (if any) as are specified in, or ascertained in accordance with, the regulations. Note: The civil remedy provisions in Part 3-7 may apply to a contravention of this section.  Schedule 1  Stored communications"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "eb977632906a901bd334ef3b8c91a786949295acd19b5e9de467daad459926cb" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-10 ;
    cof:pageNumber "14"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Court must consider regulations when determining reasonableness of actions." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
