concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-111-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "111(2) Form of applications"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-111-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) However, a person making the application on the agency’s behalf may make the application by telephone if the person:  (a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to whom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under subsection (3); and  (b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make the application by telephone." ;
    skos:definition "(2) However, a person making the application on the agency’s behalf may make the application by telephone if the person:  (a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to whom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under subsection (3); and  (b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make the application by telephone."@en ;
