doc:sch-1-sec-121 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "121 What happens when stored communications warrants are" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "issued  The chief officer of the agency must cause:  (a) the Managing Director of the carrier that holds the stored communications to which the warrant relates to be informed forthwith of the issue of the warrant; and  (b) a copy of the warrant, certified in writing by a certifying officer of the agency to be a true copy of the warrant, to be given as soon as practicable to the Managing Director of that carrier." ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-122 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "122 Revocation of stored communications warrants by chief officers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-122 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The chief officer of an enforcement agency to which a stored communications warrant has been issued must, on being satisfied that the grounds on which the warrant was issued have ceased to exist:  (a) cause the chief officer of any other enforcement agency that is exercising authority under the warrant to be informed forthwith of the proposed revocation of the warrant; and  (b) by writing signed by him or her, revoke the warrant.  Stored communications  Schedule 1 Principal amendments  Part 1  Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   19  (2) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may at any time, by writing signed by him or her, revoke a warrant issued to the agency after causing the chief officer of any other enforcement agency that is exercising authority under the warrant to be informed forthwith that the chief officer proposes to revoke the warrant.  (3) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may delegate his or her power under subsection (2) to a certifying officer of the agency.  (4) This section does not apply in relation to a warrant that has ceased to be in force." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The chief officer of an enforcement agency to which a stored communications warrant has been issued must, on being satisfied that the grounds on which the warrant was issued have ceased to exist:  (a) cause the chief officer of any other enforcement agency that is exercising authority under the warrant to be informed forthwith of the proposed revocation of the warrant; and  (b) by writing signed by him or her, revoke the warrant.  Stored communications  Schedule 1 Principal amendments  Part 1  Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   19  (2) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may at any time, by writing signed by him or her, revoke a warrant issued to the agency after causing the chief officer of any other enforcement agency that is exercising authority under the warrant to be informed forthwith that the chief officer proposes to revoke the warrant.  (3) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may delegate his or her power under subsection (2) to a certifying officer of the agency.  (4) This section does not apply in relation to a warrant that has ceased to be in force."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2cecbdcc77ce66db1b9402a98f0db0da6d348afdb185edf1544de19203c5cb18" ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-122-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-122-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-122-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-122-ss-4 ;
