doc:sch-1-sec-124 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "124 Access to additional telecommunications services under stored" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "communications warrants  (1) If:  (a) the Managing Director of a carrier has been informed, under section 121, of the issue of a stored communications warrant; and  (b) it is proposed, under the warrant, to access stored communications that, immediately before they became stored communications, had passed over a telecommunications service operated by a carrier; and  Schedule 1  Stored communications" ;
    cof:pageNumber "23"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-20 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "20 Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-20 ;
    values:originalText "(c) the service was not identified in the warrant; the chief officer must cause the Managing Director of the carrier to be given, as soon as practicable, a description in writing of the service sufficient to identify it.  (2) If:  (a) the Managing Director of a carrier has been informed, under subsection (1) of the issue of a stored communications warrant; and  (b) the chief officer of the agency to which the warrant was issued, or a certifying officer of that agency, is satisfied that it is no longer necessary to access stored communications that, immediately before they became stored communications, had passed over that service; the chief officer or the certifying officer must cause:  (c) the Managing Director to be informed forthwith of the fact; and  (d) confirmation in writing of the fact to be given as soon as practicable to the Managing Director." ;
    skos:definition "(c) the service was not identified in the warrant; the chief officer must cause the Managing Director of the carrier to be given, as soon as practicable, a description in writing of the service sufficient to identify it.  (2) If:  (a) the Managing Director of a carrier has been informed, under subsection (1) of the issue of a stored communications warrant; and  (b) the chief officer of the agency to which the warrant was issued, or a certifying officer of that agency, is satisfied that it is no longer necessary to access stored communications that, immediately before they became stored communications, had passed over that service; the chief officer or the certifying officer must cause:  (c) the Managing Director to be informed forthwith of the fact; and  (d) confirmation in writing of the fact to be given as soon as practicable to the Managing Director."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6b8657b6c84d1124a182ba141f4b653f52304f81bfc2edac4fd5d87e8c20eee2" ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Chief officer must inform Managing Director of carrier about changes in service identification." ;
    dc:description "Confirmation in writing" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
