    values:originalText "(c) the service was not identified in the warrant; the chief officer must cause the Managing Director of the carrier to be given, as soon as practicable, a description in writing of the service sufficient to identify it.  (2) If:  (a) the Managing Director of a carrier has been informed, under subsection (1) of the issue of a stored communications warrant; and  (b) the chief officer of the agency to which the warrant was issued, or a certifying officer of that agency, is satisfied that it is no longer necessary to access stored communications that, immediately before they became stored communications, had passed over that service; the chief officer or the certifying officer must cause:  (c) the Managing Director to be informed forthwith of the fact; and  (d) confirmation in writing of the fact to be given as soon as practicable to the Managing Director." ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer .

