doc:sch-1-sec-126 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "126 Limit on authority conferred by warrant" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "A stored communications warrant does not authorise access to stored communications unless notification of the issue of the warrant has been received under section 121 by or on behalf of the Managing Director of the carrier holding the stored communications." ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-127 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "127 Exercise of authority conferred by warrant"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-127 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The authority conferred by a stored communications warrant must not be exercised by a person who is not an officer or staff member of an enforcement agency in relation to whom an approval under subsection (2) is in force in relation to the warrant.  Stored communications  Schedule 1 Principal amendments  Part 1  Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   21  (2) The chief officer of an agency, or an officer of an agency in relation to whom an appointment under subsection (3) is in force, may approve any of the following to exercise the authority conferred by warrants, or classes of warrants, issued to the agency:  (a) officers or staff members of the agency;  (b) classes of officers or staff members of the agency;  (c) officers or staff members of another enforcement agency;  (d) classes of officers or staff members of another enforcement agency.  (3) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may appoint in writing an officer of the agency to be an approving officer for the purposes of subsection (2)." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The authority conferred by a stored communications warrant must not be exercised by a person who is not an officer or staff member of an enforcement agency in relation to whom an approval under subsection (2) is in force in relation to the warrant.  Stored communications  Schedule 1 Principal amendments  Part 1  Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   21  (2) The chief officer of an agency, or an officer of an agency in relation to whom an appointment under subsection (3) is in force, may approve any of the following to exercise the authority conferred by warrants, or classes of warrants, issued to the agency:  (a) officers or staff members of the agency;  (b) classes of officers or staff members of the agency;  (c) officers or staff members of another enforcement agency;  (d) classes of officers or staff members of another enforcement agency.  (3) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may appoint in writing an officer of the agency to be an approving officer for the purposes of subsection (2)."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bea55b00b47eeef2dbec834687a4e145d49a734b0963e17b1695b1116c3ca7af" ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-127-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-127-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-127-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.24" .
