concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-24 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "24 Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-24 ;
    values:originalText "(iii) makes a record of information; or  (iv) gives information in evidence in a proceeding; and  (b) the information is:  (i) lawfully accessed information; or  (ii) information obtained by accessing a stored communication in contravention of subsection 108(1); or  (iii) stored communications warrant information. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units, or both.  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to conduct permitted under this Part. Note 1: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in subsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code). Note 2: The civil remedy provisions in Part 3-7 may apply to a contravention of this section." ;
    skos:definition "(iii) makes a record of information; or  (iv) gives information in evidence in a proceeding; and  (b) the information is:  (i) lawfully accessed information; or  (ii) information obtained by accessing a stored communication in contravention of subsection 108(1); or  (iii) stored communications warrant information. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units, or both.  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to conduct permitted under this Part. Note 1: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in subsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code). Note 2: The civil remedy provisions in Part 3-7 may apply to a contravention of this section."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6dc8e9c4f7029d242ea2b3c8e92cbf9d8ce39bc028dfd1018b0b09f105cf526a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "28"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Making or giving information in evidence without lawful access is prohibited." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.28" ;
    cml:asserts concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-24-norm .
