concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-136 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "136 Dealing in connection with Organisation’s functions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-136 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person may, in connection with the performance by the Organisation of its functions, or otherwise for purposes of security, communicate to another person, make use of, or make a record of the following:  (a) lawfully accessed information other than foreign intelligence information;  (b) stored communications warrant information.  (2) The Director-General of Security may, in connection with the performance by the Organisation of its functions, communicate foreign intelligence information to an officer or employee of the Organisation.  (3) An officer or employee of the Organisation may, in connection with the performance by the Organisation of its functions, communicate foreign intelligence information to the Director-General of Security or to another such officer or employee.  (4) The Director-General of Security or an officer or employee of the Organisation may, in connection with the performance by the Organisation of its functions, make use of, or make a record of, foreign intelligence information.  Stored communications  Schedule 1 Principal amendments  Part 1  Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   27" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person may, in connection with the performance by the Organisation of its functions, or otherwise for purposes of security, communicate to another person, make use of, or make a record of the following:  (a) lawfully accessed information other than foreign intelligence information;  (b) stored communications warrant information.  (2) The Director-General of Security may, in connection with the performance by the Organisation of its functions, communicate foreign intelligence information to an officer or employee of the Organisation.  (3) An officer or employee of the Organisation may, in connection with the performance by the Organisation of its functions, communicate foreign intelligence information to the Director-General of Security or to another such officer or employee.  (4) The Director-General of Security or an officer or employee of the Organisation may, in connection with the performance by the Organisation of its functions, make use of, or make a record of, foreign intelligence information.  Stored communications  Schedule 1 Principal amendments  Part 1  Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   27"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "22110b330f00bea35aae19b9883b3b04fdb6e7870706c244fcf66657ab10b530" ;
    cof:pageNumber "30"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-136-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-136-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-136-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-136-ss-4 ;
