    values:originalText "(1) The Director-General of Security may, in accordance with paragraph 18(3)(a) or (b) of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979, communicate the following to another person:  (a) lawfully accessed information;  (b) stored communications warrant information.  (2) The communication may be made by the Director-General of Security personally or by a person authorised by the Director-General.  (3) A person to whom foreign intelligence information has been communicated:  (a) in accordance with subsection (1); or  (b) in accordance with an approval given under this subsection; may communicate that information to such persons, and in such manner, as are approved in writing by the Attorney-General." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Director-General of Security may, in accordance with paragraph 18(3)(a) or (b) of the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979, communicate the following to another person:  (a) lawfully accessed information;  (b) stored communications warrant information.  (2) The communication may be made by the Director-General of Security personally or by a person authorised by the Director-General.  (3) A person to whom foreign intelligence information has been communicated:  (a) in accordance with subsection (1); or  (b) in accordance with an approval given under this subsection; may communicate that information to such persons, and in such manner, as are approved in writing by the Attorney-General."@en ;
