concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-30 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "30 Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-30 ;
    values:originalText "(2) A person to whom the information is communicated in accordance with subsection (1) may communicate to another person, make use of, or make a record of, some or all of the information for a purpose (or 2 or more purposes) connected with:  (a) an investigation of a suspected offence; or  (b) the making by an authority, body or person of a decision whether or not to begin a proceeding by way of a prosecution for a suspected offence; or  (c) a proceeding by way of a prosecution for a suspected offence; and for no other purpose." ;
    skos:definition "(2) A person to whom the information is communicated in accordance with subsection (1) may communicate to another person, make use of, or make a record of, some or all of the information for a purpose (or 2 or more purposes) connected with:  (a) an investigation of a suspected offence; or  (b) the making by an authority, body or person of a decision whether or not to begin a proceeding by way of a prosecution for a suspected offence; or  (c) a proceeding by way of a prosecution for a suspected offence; and for no other purpose."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "38e397c633487c256494dddc10dcf18148b59c4dae8600b5ecadaf97f483a8d1" ;
    cof:pageNumber "34"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Communicating intercepted information for specific purposes." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
