concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-143 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "143 Giving information in evidence in exempt proceeding"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-143 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person may give lawfully accessed information (other than foreign intelligence information) in evidence in an exempt proceeding.  (2) For the purposes of applying subsection (1) in relation to information, the question whether or not a stored communication  Stored communications  Schedule 1 Principal amendments  Part 1  Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   31 was accessed in contravention of subsection 108(1) may be determined on the balance of probabilities.  (3) A person may give stored communications warrant information in evidence in an exempt proceeding." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person may give lawfully accessed information (other than foreign intelligence information) in evidence in an exempt proceeding.  (2) For the purposes of applying subsection (1) in relation to information, the question whether or not a stored communication  Stored communications  Schedule 1 Principal amendments  Part 1  Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   31 was accessed in contravention of subsection 108(1) may be determined on the balance of probabilities.  (3) A person may give stored communications warrant information in evidence in an exempt proceeding."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ca1938734b630f54d272e4bf3ffb003dbe0641d72bba2849db7c12eedfe12803" ;
    cof:pageNumber "34"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-143-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-143-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-143-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
