concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-146 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "146 Giving information in evidence in civil proceedings for remedial"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-146 ;
    values:originalText "relief  (1) A person may give information obtained by accessing a stored communication in contravention of subsection 108(1) in evidence in a proceeding by way of an application under section 165 for remedial relief in respect of:  (a) the access; or  (b) the communication (in contravention of section 133) of information obtained by the access.  (2) A person may give stored communications warrant information in evidence in a proceeding by way of an application under section 165." ;
    skos:definition "relief  (1) A person may give information obtained by accessing a stored communication in contravention of subsection 108(1) in evidence in a proceeding by way of an application under section 165 for remedial relief in respect of:  (a) the access; or  (b) the communication (in contravention of section 133) of information obtained by the access.  (2) A person may give stored communications warrant information in evidence in a proceeding by way of an application under section 165."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ea6a344e27604dcb67a09c548bcf44b13628c54debf48bcf37139db8f9f9dd86" ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-146-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-146-ss-2 ;
