concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-34 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "34 Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-34 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The chief officer must, as soon as practicable, and in any event within 3 months, after each 30 June, give to the Minister a written report that sets out the extent to which information and records were destroyed in accordance with this section." ;
    skos:definition "(2) The chief officer must, as soon as practicable, and in any event within 3 months, after each 30 June, give to the Minister a written report that sets out the extent to which information and records were destroyed in accordance with this section."@en ;
