    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "of warrants  The chief officer of an enforcement agency must cause to be kept in the agency’s records:  (a) each stored communications warrant issued to the agency; and  (b) each instrument revoking such a warrant; and  (c) a copy of each certificate issued under subsection 130(1) by a certifying officer of the agency; and  (d) each authorisation by the chief officer under subsection 135(2); and  (e) particulars of the destruction of information and records that the chief officer has caused in accordance with section 150." ;
