concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-152 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "152 Functions of Ombudsman"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-152 ;
    values:originalText "Subject to this Division, the Ombudsman has the following additional functions:  (a) to inspect an enforcement agency’s records in order to ascertain, so far as is practicable, the extent of compliance, in relation to those records, with sections 150 and 151; and  (b) to report to the Minister about the results of inspections under this Division; and  (c) to do anything incidental or conducive to the performance of any of the preceding functions.  Stored communications  Schedule 1 Principal amendments  Part 1  Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   35" ;
    skos:definition "Subject to this Division, the Ombudsman has the following additional functions:  (a) to inspect an enforcement agency’s records in order to ascertain, so far as is practicable, the extent of compliance, in relation to those records, with sections 150 and 151; and  (b) to report to the Minister about the results of inspections under this Division; and  (c) to do anything incidental or conducive to the performance of any of the preceding functions.  Stored communications  Schedule 1 Principal amendments  Part 1  Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   35"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "794adb6d1ad2c45c54ff0556820dac6677c61f26d7ca927cdedbfc4a93a714c8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "38"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Inspect enforcement agency records to ascertain compliance with sections 150 and 151." ;
