concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-170 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "170 Extended meaning of conviction—orders under section 19B of"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-170 ;
    values:originalText "the Crimes Act 1914  A reference in this Part to the conviction of a person of an offence includes a reference to the making of an order under section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 in relation to a person in respect of an offence. Note: Section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 empowers a court that has found a person to have committed an offence to take action without proceeding to record a conviction.  Stored communications  Schedule 1 Other amendments  Part 2  Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   45" ;
    skos:definition "the Crimes Act 1914  A reference in this Part to the conviction of a person of an offence includes a reference to the making of an order under section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 in relation to a person in respect of an offence. Note: Section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 empowers a court that has found a person to have committed an offence to take action without proceeding to record a conviction.  Stored communications  Schedule 1 Other amendments  Part 2  Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   45"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ab535d01ceb39ecc7a3c1e2e754f132df4a30b77ca67d73e6f716898b8ce3ef4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "48"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "A reference in this Part to the conviction of a person of an offence includes a reference to the making of an order under section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 in relation to a person in respect of an offence." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
