doc:sch-3-sec-9-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "9(1) Subsection 11B(1)" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Attorney-General may, under his or her hand, issue a warrant in respect of a person if:  (a) the Director-General of Security gives a notice in writing to the Attorney-General requesting the Attorney-General to issue a warrant under this section authorising persons approved under section 12 in respect of the warrant to do acts or things referred to in subsection 9A(1A) in relation to:  Equipment-based interception  Schedule 3  Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   71  (i) communications that are being made to or from any telecommunications service that a person or foreign organisation is using, or is likely to use; or  (ii) communications that are being made by means of a particular telecommunications device that a person or foreign organisation is using, or is likely to use;  for the purpose of obtaining foreign intelligence relating to a matter specified in the notice; and  (b) the Attorney-General is satisfied, on the basis of advice received from the relevant Minister, that:  (i) the obtaining of foreign intelligence relating to that matter is important in relation to the defence of the Commonwealth or to the conduct of the Commonwealth’s international affairs; and  (ii) it is necessary to intercept the communications of the person or foreign organisation in order to obtain the intelligence referred to in paragraph (a); and  (iii) relying on a telecommunications service warrant to obtain the intelligence would be ineffective." ;
    cof:pageNumber "74"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-3-sec-9-ss-1a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "9(1A) Subsection 11B(1)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-9-ss-1a ;
    values:originalText "(1A) The warrant authorises persons approved under section 12 in respect of the warrant to intercept, subject to any conditions or restrictions that are specified in the warrant:  (a) communications that are being made to or from any telecommunications service that the person or foreign organisation is using, or is likely to use; or  (b) communications that are being made by means of a telecommunications device, identified in the warrant, that the person or foreign organisation is using, or is likely to use. Note: Subsection (3) restricts the issuing of a warrant authorising interception of communications made by means of a telecommunications device identified in the warrant." ;
    skos:definition "(1A) The warrant authorises persons approved under section 12 in respect of the warrant to intercept, subject to any conditions or restrictions that are specified in the warrant:  (a) communications that are being made to or from any telecommunications service that the person or foreign organisation is using, or is likely to use; or  (b) communications that are being made by means of a telecommunications device, identified in the warrant, that the person or foreign organisation is using, or is likely to use. Note: Subsection (3) restricts the issuing of a warrant authorising interception of communications made by means of a telecommunications device identified in the warrant."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "04c0704898add688faa38b36bef400c457a17f405133a4e25022edf2afeaf4f3" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-3-sec-9 ;
    cof:pageNumber "74"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Authorises interception of communications under specified conditions." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf> ;
