concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-5-sec-11 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "11 Subsections 57(1) and (2)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-5-sec-11 ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsections, substitute:  (1) The chief officer of an agency must, on being satisfied that the grounds on which a warrant was issued to the agency have ceased to exist:  (a) cause the Secretary of the Department to be informed forthwith that the chief officer proposes to revoke the warrant; and  (b) cause the chief officer of any other agency that is exercising authority under the warrant to be informed forthwith of the proposed revocation of the warrant; and  (c) by writing signed by him or her, revoke the warrant.  (2) The chief officer of an agency may at any time, by writing signed by him or her, revoke a warrant issued to the agency after:  (a) causing the Secretary of the Department to be informed of the proposed revocation; and  (b) causing the chief officer of any other agency that is exercising authority under the warrant to be informed  Schedule 5  Transfer of functions" ;
    skos:definition "Repeal the subsections, substitute:  (1) The chief officer of an agency must, on being satisfied that the grounds on which a warrant was issued to the agency have ceased to exist:  (a) cause the Secretary of the Department to be informed forthwith that the chief officer proposes to revoke the warrant; and  (b) cause the chief officer of any other agency that is exercising authority under the warrant to be informed forthwith of the proposed revocation of the warrant; and  (c) by writing signed by him or her, revoke the warrant.  (2) The chief officer of an agency may at any time, by writing signed by him or her, revoke a warrant issued to the agency after:  (a) causing the Secretary of the Department to be informed of the proposed revocation; and  (b) causing the chief officer of any other agency that is exercising authority under the warrant to be informed  Schedule 5  Transfer of functions"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "45006b563b2fa2182b7ea81cca2aac16faa404d7946d1c0f51f91fbff6cf069d" ;
    cof:pageNumber "87"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-5-sec-11-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-5-sec-11-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.87" .
doc:sch-5-sec-11 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "11 Subsections 57(1) and (2)" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Repeal the subsections, substitute:  (1) The chief officer of an agency must, on being satisfied that the grounds on which a warrant was issued to the agency have ceased to exist:  (a) cause the Secretary of the Department to be informed forthwith that the chief officer proposes to revoke the warrant; and  (b) cause the chief officer of any other agency that is exercising authority under the warrant to be informed forthwith of the proposed revocation of the warrant; and  (c) by writing signed by him or her, revoke the warrant.  (2) The chief officer of an agency may at any time, by writing signed by him or her, revoke a warrant issued to the agency after:  (a) causing the Secretary of the Department to be informed of the proposed revocation; and  (b) causing the chief officer of any other agency that is exercising authority under the warrant to be informed  Schedule 5  Transfer of functions" ;
    cof:pageNumber "87"^^xsd:integer .

